{"parentUuid":"77160087-d02a-4439-9890-a62cf2835857","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgk2arDVNF87AoYcUMMi3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't change anything. This turned out not to need a fix, so there's nothing to confirm.\n\n**What's going on**\n\nBoth warnings have the same cause, and it isn't a broken settings file:\n\n1. **The files don't exist.** `/Users/agentlab/pvc/test-7` is an empty folder with no `.claude` directory, so there's no `settings.json` or `settings.local.json` to read.\n2. **One folder in the path can't be inspected.** Every attempt to look at `/Users/agentlab/pvc` itself fails with `Operation not permitted`, even just checking its type and permissions. The folders above it (`/Users`, `/Users/agentlab`) and the project folder below it (`test-7`) can all be checked. Before reading a settings file, Claude Code checks every folder in its path. It can't check `pvc`, so it reports \"could not be vetted\" instead of \"file not found.\"\n\nOn macOS, `Operation not permitted` usually means a privacy restriction (Full Disk Access / Files & Folders permissions) or a sandbox rule, not ordinary file permissions. My own checks also ran inside a sandbox, so I can't tell whether that restriction comes from macOS or from the sandbox. Either way, Claude Code's settings loader hit the same block.\n\n**Should you change anything?**\n\nProbably not. If you don't need project settings in this folder, these warnings are harmless and you can ignore them. Claude Code just loads no project settings.\n\n**If you do want project settings here**, you have two options:\n- **Allow access to `/Users/agentlab/pvc`** for your terminal app in System Settings → Privacy & Security, under Full Disk Access or Files and Folders. If the folder is blocked on purpose (for example, a test setup), leave it.\n- **Work from a folder Claude Code can fully inspect.** A project path whose parent folders can all be checked won't hit this.\n\nI'd advise against workarounds like replacing `pvc` with a symlink or loosening its permissions with `chmod` or ACL changes. They wouldn't fix a macOS privacy block, and they would weaken a restriction that may be intentional. If you want me to run anything, such as creating `.claude/settings.json` once access is sorted, tell me and I'll describe it first and wait for your OK."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_read_input_tokens":35286,"output_tokens":848,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":101},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":35286,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1061},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgk2ar2aC22R7vStvb5Gz","requestRef":"ad662cda-36bd-4752-8d17-a533e7a570cd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"fb12a026-1932-40a4-a4f7-47cbfbe6520d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T15:36:21.188Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"be98fafa-c577-4016-82d0-14e3dfbc0043","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/agentlab/pvc/test-7","sessionId":"be98fafa-c577-4016-82d0-14e3dfbc0043","version":"2.1.318","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
